# A prompt chunk's sparse latent attention (latent._sparse_onepass) as a CUDA kernel (sparse_onepass.cu) that computes
# every output with the Triton kernel's own instruction sequence, read from its PTX: the mma chains and their K order,
# the online softmax's roundings and ex2.approx, the p-sum's reduction tree, div.full. Keys as the mma's M side (the
# GB10's mma.sync is operand-symmetric bit for bit), q in registers, softmax inside a warp, producer warps gathering and
# converting the FP8 rows two tiles ahead, five P.V warps balancing the SM's four schedulers. Every output is the Triton
# kernel's bit for bit. FP8 caches and 17-24 heads a rank only (TP=3's 22 / 21: the kernel holds 24 heads in three QK
# warps); TP=2's 32 heads keep Triton. Built / loaded by decode.Engine's constructor like patch 0105's, and like it
# not used (logged once; the Triton kernel serves) under another Triton release than sparse.TRITON_PTX (3.7) or when
# the build fails. TF_GLM_ONEPASS_CUDA=0: the Triton kernel. Applies after patch 0105 (decode.py's start-up loads, and
# sparse.TRITON_PTX). tools/sparse_onepass_check.py.

